{"archetypes":[{"name":"rename-propagation","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan claims only one production sourcer references voter_coverage_* but does not audit test harnesses, Makefile targets, CI configs, or documentation outside the explicit file list — a missed call-site will break at runtime rather than at plan-review time.","prompt_body":"Audit the plan's rename claim against the full repo corpus by searching for every variant of voter_coverage_ and lib-voter-coverage in scripts/, skills/, .claude/, docs/, Makefile, .github/, and agent definition files. Verify that the plan's file list accounts for all hits, including any existing test harness for the old library (e.g. test-lib-voter-coverage.sh), Makefile targets that invoke or lint the old filename, and CI workflow steps that reference it. Check whether the plan includes an explicit deletion step for the old lib-voter-coverage.sh and lib-voter-coverage.md files — without it, both filenames coexist and a sourcer could pick either silently depending on eval order. Confirm that any file outside the plan's explicit list that cites the old doc name by path (cross-references in other .md files, topology.tsv, README.md) is also covered by the plan. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"allowlist-logic","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan's allowlist-matching algorithm has three unresolved correctness risks — trailing-slash normalization, glob-special characters in the pattern side of case, and silent cd failure — that are acknowledged but not fully specified in the plan text.","prompt_body":"Examine the plan's description of larch_design_tmpdir_validate for internal logical gaps: the plan acknowledges a trailing-slash mismatch failure mode and says to normalize with ${tmpdir%/}/ at allowlist construction time, but does not show whether the case pattern side is also quoted to suppress glob expansion when $TMPDIR contains brackets or asterisks. Verify whether cd \"$parent\" && pwd -P has an explicit guard in the plan's step-by-step algorithm — the plan says 'returns 2' on permission denial but the described sequence does not show the conditional exit after the cd step. Check whether the plan's use of $'\\n' and $'\\r' ANSI-C quoting in the emit_kv case pattern position is documented as Bash 3.2-safe; ANSI-C quoting in case pattern position has known portability notes on macOS Bash 3.2.57 that the plan does not address. Evaluate whether the test harness plan for lib-design-tmpdir.sh actually exercises the symlink case where only the leaf component (not the parent) is a symlink pointing outside the allowlist, since the plan's resolution algorithm canonicalizes only the parent directory. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
